Subject: iOS: switch off the new desktop-only surface of c18645860

docs/ios-deadlist.md, the c18645860 rows. The things the 1,282-commit bump
brought that a phone cannot use, each gated at the one place both its menu
row and its automatic path go through:

  update.c        updateIsAvailable() is false on iOS. With curl linked (D-010)
                  it answered true, which was harmless while the only way in
                  was the hidden Check for Updates row; the new update NOTICE
                  (updatemenu.c, updatenoticeStart from main.c) asks GitHub at
                  every launch and opens a "new version" dialog on the main
                  menu offering to install a desktop build.
  patchnotes.c    the once-after-an-update patch notes popup never opens: it is
                  Dab's desktop changelog (and an install whose pd.ini predates
                  the notes gets every entry), not this app's release notes.
  optionsmenu.c   Video > Renderer is hidden: one renderer here, and it is
                  ANGLE-Metal rather than the "OpenGL" the row names (Vulkan is
                  never built for iOS, PD_VULKAN=OFF in build-ios.sh).
                  Advanced > HiDPI Window and HIDAPI Controllers are hidden:
                  0017 forces the native drawable whatever AllowHiDpi says, and
                  the shell forces HIDAPI off (D-030). Raw Input stays hidden as
                  upstream hides it off Windows.
                  Video > SMAA, Upscaling, Supersampling and FSR Sharpness are
                  hidden, and Anti-aliasing loses its TAA entry: upstream's own
                  post chain does not run on GL ES (gfx_opengl_post_process:
                  "SMAA and FSR need desktop GL 3.0, off"; gfx_pc: "TAA could
                  not run on this renderer, off" - both seen on lane 3), so the
                  rows were switches that did nothing, or a render scale with a
                  plain blit under an FSR name. The shell owns render scale.

Every hunk is PLATFORM_IOS-gated; no other platform changes by a byte.

